{
  "name": "A · Loan product discovery",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0a0a0a0a-0000-4000-8000-000000000101",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1312,
        "height": 256,
        "content": "## A · Loan product discovery (S1 crawl-time compile + S6 confidence guard)\nDaily at 06:00, or run manually. For each source in `crawl_sources`, one at a time: check robots.txt → fetch pages → clean to structured text → SHA-256 → **unchanged? skip the LLM**. Otherwise extract through the LLM gateway → validate and compile rules in code → upsert with a criteria diff → close the crawl run.\n`crawl_mode=fixtures` (default) reads saved pages from the `fixtures` container. `live` fetches the real sites with our User-Agent and a pause between requests.\nEvery failure path closes that source's run as `error`, so one bad source never stops the others.\nLast, **Warm match cache** judges every cohort the active products can produce, so Workflow B finds them cached and makes no LLM call at match time.\n**A second run skips the LLM by design** (pages unchanged, cohorts cached). `make demo-reset` forgets one page's hash and the warm cache, so the next run takes every branch."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0a0a0a0a-0000-4000-8000-000000000102",
      "name": "Per-source error handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1504,
        672
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 2560,
        "height": 160,
        "color": 3,
        "content": "### Failure paths\nrobots.txt disallowed or unreachable · a page not 200 · the LLM failed or the budget is spent · validation threw · upsert failed. Each one becomes an item with `run_status` and `error`, and goes to **Finish crawl run**, which records it in `crawl_runs`. Then the loop moves on to the next source."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0a0a0a0a-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Daily at 06:00",
